      "title": "Research Instructor, Research Assistant Professor, Research Associate Professor, Research Professor, Assistant Professor, Associate Professor, Professor",
      "description": "East Carolina University Portal | Research Instructor, Research Assistant Professor, Research Associate Professor, Research Professor, Assistant Professor, Associate Professor, Professor Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Applicant Interest Card Notifications Log In /Create Account Help Applicants Have Rights Under Federal Employment Laws Immigration Law Related Notices Relocation Assistance Program Working at ECU Research Instructor, Research Assistant Professor, Research Associate Professor, Research Professor, Assistant Professor, Associate Professor, Professor Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. To apply, please submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, a statement of research interests , a statement of teaching philosophy , and contact information for three references through ECU’s online job application portal. At the time of employment, three original letters of reference, official transcripts, a criminal background check, and proper documentation of identity and employability are required. Please be aware that if selected for an interview, an automatic e-mail will be sent to the individuals entered by the applicant in the References Section of the PeopleAdmin applicant tracking system. Letters of reference submitted via the PeopleAdmin applicant tracking system will be verified and considered towards meeting this requirement. Posting Details Position Information Job Title Research Instructor, Research Assistant Professor, Research Associate Professor, Research Professor, Assistant Professor, Associate Professor, Professor Position Number 600237 Vacancy Open to All Candidates Department EHH BSOM Physiology Department Homepage https://physiology.ecu.edu/ Advertising Department PHYSIOLOGY Division ECU Health/BSOM Classification Title Research Instructor, Research Assistant Professor, Research Associate Professor, Research Professor, Assistant Professor, Associate Professor, Professor Working Title Research Instructor, Research Assistant Professor, Research Associate Professor, Research Professor, Assistant Professor, Associate Professor, Professor Number of Vacancies 4 Full Time Equivalent (FTE) 1.0 Full Time or Part Time Full Time Anticipated Recruitment Range. Salary offered may be outside of this range as impacted by budget, UNC salary administration, and/or candidate qualifications. Commensurate with Qualifications Position Location (City) Greenville Position Type Faculty (Teaching) Job Category Faculty (Teaching) Be a Pirate! Be a Pirate! East Carolina University ( ECU ) is consistently ranked among the nation’s top public universities for its commitment to research, innovation, social mobility, and public service. Classified as a R1 institution by the Carnegie Commission on Higher Education, ECU is among the top 5% of research universities in the United States, an elite designation reflecting the highest levels of research activity, funding, and doctoral output. Founded in 1907, ECU is a public, four-year university located in Greenville, N.C. , which is widely regarded as the cultural, educational, economic, and medical hub of eastern North Carolina. Through education, research, healthcare, community engagement, athletics, cultural enrichment, and service, ECU enhances the quality of life for its students, the state and communities around the world. It is a great place to work, teach, and learn. ECU’s commitment to impactful scholarship is further demonstrated through its repeated Carnegie Community Engagement Classification (2010, 2015, 2024), as well as its 2024 designation as a Carnegie Leadership for Public Purpose institution. These distinctions recognize the university’s leadership in translating research into meaningful community partnerships and measurable societal benefits. The university supports its workforce through a wide range of professional development opportunities designed to foster career growth and skill advancement. Eligible employees also benefit from a comprehensive benefits package that promotes a healthy work-life balance. Organizational Unit Overview The Department of Physiology at the Brody School of Medicine, East Carolina University, is dedicated to advancing the understanding of physiology through excellence in education of medical and graduate students; to perform innovative and groundbreaking research in its related sub-disciplines; to promote and inspire discovery and learning that enhances patient care; and to contribute to the translation of scientific progress into clinical practice. The Department of Physiology consists of full-time, 12-month state-funded faculty, research technicians, postdoctoral fellows, administrative staff, and students. The department delivers foundational instruction in integrative physiology to a wide range of learners, including medical, dental, nursing, and graduate students, and maintains a strong educational mission focused on preparing healthcare professionals and researchers with a comprehensive understanding of physiological systems. This foundation supports specialized clinical and research careers aimed at addressing functional aspects of human physiology and disease. The department’s Ph.D. program in Biomedical Sciences provides rigorous, interdisciplinary training that prepares graduates for a variety of leadership roles in academia, research, government, industry, and medicine. Job Duties The Department of Physiology at the Brody School of Medicine ( BSOM ), East Carolina University ( ECU ), invites applications for open rank full-time, 12-month faculty positions, including at the rank of Research Instructor, Research Assistant Professor, Research Associate Professor, Research Professor (fixed-term, non-tenure track), and Assistant/Associate/Professor (tenure-track) . Rank and track will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. Research instructor (fixed-term) - Teaching 5% (training technicians, undergraduate and graduate students, and junior research associates), service 5% (serve on student advisory committees as needed), research 90% (includes performing literature reviews; developing studies; experimental design; performing experiments; collecting, analyzing, and interpreting data; writing abstracts and manuscripts; presenting data at regional, national or international conferences; and writing grant proposals). Research Assistant Professor (fixed-term) – Teaching 2-5% (training technicians and/or students), Service 5% (serve on student advisory committees as needed), and Research 90-93% (develop and establish an independent research program at ECU , disseminate research results through publications and presentations in national and international venues, secure extramural funding for their research program). Research Associate Professor (fixed-term) – Teaching 5% (training technicians and/or mentor/advise trainees and/or students), Service 5% (serve on department level committees), and Research 90% (develop and establish an independent research program at ECU , disseminate research results through publications and presentations in national and international venues, secure extramural funding for their research program). Research Professor (fixed-term) – Teaching 5-10% (training technicians and/or mentor/advise students and postdoctoral fellows), Service 5-10% (serve on department level and/or school level committees), and Research 80-90% (develop and establish an independent research program at ECU , disseminate research results through publications and presentations in national and international venues, secure extramural funding for their research program). Assistant Professor (tenure-track) – Teaching 5% (teaching graduate course work and mentoring/advising students), service 5% (serve in departmental committees), research 90% (develop and establish an independent research program at ECU , disseminate research results through publications and presentations in national and international venues, secure extramural funding for their research program) Associate Professor (tenure-track) – Teaching 20% (teach and/or be course director for graduate and medical courses, mentor/advise students), service 10% (serve in departmental and school committees), research 70% (establish their research program at ECU , disseminate research results through publications and presentations in national and international venues, secure extramural funding for their research program) Professor (tenure-track) – Teaching 35% (teach and/or be course director for graduate and medical courses, mentor/advise students), service 20% (serve in departmental, school, and university committees), research 45% (establish their research program at ECU , disseminate research results through publications and presentations in national and international venues, secure extramural funding for their research program) Research Environment: State-of-the-art research facilities support research within the department and emphasize areas such as cardiovascular science, neuroscience, and cell physiology. Faculty members are engaged in both foundational and translational research and mentor/train medical, graduate, and professional students. Faculty within the Physiology Department collaborate extensively with colleagues across ECU and with external academic institutions, government entities, and industry partners. The department has a strong track record of interdisciplinary research and a consistent history of securing extramural funding. Research instructors will join dynamic labs with distinguished and established research programs. Tenure-track positions will be supported by generous laboratory space, state salary support, and a competitive research start-up package. Applicants conducting high-impact research in any area of physiology are encouraged to apply. Contingent upon the availability of funds Minimum Education/Experience A Ph.D., M.D., or equivalent in Physiology, Biomedical Sciences, or a related field. Relevant teaching experience along with the following: A strong background in physiology and/or biomedical sciences . Documented experience in teaching and/or mentoring students, conducting independent or collaborative research , and participating in departmental or professional service activities. Record of contributing to research initiatives that complement or broaden a department’s focus areas, as evidenced by publications, collaborations, or grant submissions. For tenure-track (Assistant Professor) candidates : the ability to establish and maintain an independent, extramurally funded research program and a record of scholarly productivity as evidenced by high-quality, peer-reviewed publications. For Associate Professor and Professor candidates : a record of extramural research funding , sustained scholarly productivity , and active participation in medical education . All degrees must be received from appropriately accredited institutions. License or Certification Required by Statute or Regulation None Preferred Experience, Skills, Training/Education Demonstrated research productivity and current or potential for extramural funding. Special Instructions to Applicant To apply, please submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, a statement of research interests , a statement of teaching philosophy , and contact information for three references through ECU’s online job application portal. At the time of employment, three original letters of reference, official transcripts, a criminal background check, and proper documentation of identity and employability are required. Please be aware that if selected for an interview, an automatic e-mail will be sent to the individuals entered by the applicant in the References Section of the PeopleAdmin applicant tracking system. Letters of reference submitted via the PeopleAdmin applicant tracking system will be verified and considered towards meeting this requirement. Additional Instructions to Applicant In order to be considered for this position, applicants must complete a candidate profile online via the PeopleAdmin system and submit any requested documents. Additionally, applicants that possess the preferred education and experience must also possess the minimum education/experience, if applicable. Unless otherwise identified in the applicable job posting and consistent with University policy, the University will principally employ individuals who reside in the State of North Carolina to the greatest extent practicable. As such, most positions at East Carolina University require employees to live and work in North Carolina (or live within a reasonable daily commuting distance from their duty station) after hire. Candidates should be prepared to relocate within a reasonable, agreed-upon time after an offer of employment has been made and accepted to meet this requirement. Job Open Date 10/27/2025 Open Until Filled Yes Job Close Date - Positions will be posted until 11:59 p.m. EST on this date. If no closing date is indicated, the position may close at any time after the initial screening date. Initial Screening Begins 11/27/2025 Rank Level Professor, Associate Professor, Assistant Professor, Instructor Quick Link for Direct Access to Posting https://ecu.peopleadmin.com/postings/88586 Nondiscrimination Statement East Carolina University is committed to workforce success and cultivating a culture of care for our employees. ECU prohibits unlawful discrimination and harassment based on race/ethnicity, color, genetic information, national origin, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, age, disability, political affiliation, and veteran status. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to their protected veteran status or disability. Individuals requesting accommodation under the Americans with Disabilities Act Amendments Act ( ADAAA ) should contact the ADA Coordinator at (252) 737-1018 (Voice/ TTY ) or ADA -Coordinator@ecu.edu . Eligibility for Employment Final candidates are subject to criminal & sex offender background checks. Some vacancies also require credit or motor vehicle checks. ECU participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Department for People Operations, Success, and Opportunity If you experience any problems accessing the system or have questions about the application process, please contact the Department for People Operations, Success, and Opportunity at (252) 328-9847 or toll free at 1-866-489-1740 or send an email to employment@ecu.edu. Our office is available to provide assistance Monday-Friday from 8:00-5:00 EST . Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Please indicate where you learned about this job vacancy. LinkedIn Chronicle of Higher Education CareerBuilder Greenville Daily Reflector Raleigh News & Observer HigherEdJobs.com InsideHigherEd.com Monster.com Indeed ECU Website Other What is the highest degree you have earned? PhD, DSC, MD, or DVM Masters Bachelors Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Curriculum Vitae/Resume Cover Letter List of References Additional Document #1 Additional Document #2 Optional Documents Transcripts Letter of Recommendation Student Employment UNC Wide Employment NC State Agencies Employment Back to top To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
